   "id": 505473,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the product of 4 and 19 modulo 12?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>First, multiply 4 and 19 to get 76.</p>\n<p>Now, find 76 mod 12.</p>\n<p>Determine the remainder when 76 is divided by 12.</p>\n<p>76 ÷ 12 = 6 and a remainder. What is that remainder?</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"12 \\times 6 = 72\"></span></p>\n<p>Subtract 72 from 76.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"76 – 72 = 4\"></span></p>\n<p>The remainder is 4.</p>\n<p>The remainder is the solution to 76 mod 12.</p>\n<p>76 mod 12 ≡ 4</p>\n<p>The product of 4 and 19 modulo 12 is 4.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "4"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
